# Offline / QA mode — used ONLY by `npm run dev:offline` (vite --mode offline).
#
# Vite layers .env.[mode] on top of .env, so these blank values override the real
# Firebase keys and the app falls back to LOCAL MODE (localStorage, everyone is admin).
# That makes it possible to exercise the UI without touching the club's live data.
#
# Why this file and not `.env.local`: `.env.local` is loaded in EVERY mode, including a
# production build — which is exactly how a Firebase-disabled build once shipped and
# looked identical to total data loss. A mode-specific file cannot leak into `npm run build`.
#
# Contains no secrets, so it is committed on purpose.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
